From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 01:40:00 -0400
Subject: first start: the local new tab page whatever the engine, no API-keys
 infobar, no theme picker

Three things the operator's first start on the Windows preview showed
(round 9, docs/ARC-ROUND2.md):

- Choosing Google on the welcome flow opened Chromium's first-party new
  tab page -- a Google surface: its logo, the OneGoogleBar, the theme and
  Web Store promos -- where every other engine got the local page.
  NewTabURLDetails::ForProfile returns the local third-party page for
  every provider now (new-tab N1; BACKLOG S-45 closed).
- "Google API keys are missing. Some functionality of Stedding will be
  disabled. Learn more" on the first window. The keys are for Google's
  services, which this browser does not use; the infobar is gone
  (welcome W9).
- Settings > Appearance offered a "Theme" row that opened Chromium's
  Customize Chrome panel, whose colours barely reach a window the Space
  tints and whose promos point at the Web Store, one of them a toast in
  white on white. The row is hidden through the page-visibility rule the
  Google sections already use (settings T12). The plain toast background
  takes the dialog colour like the prominent one, so no views toast can
  draw light text on a light ground either.

Why: docs/features/new-tab.md N1, welcome W9, settings T12.
Removable when: Chromium offers its local new tab page for Google too,
drops the API-keys infobar, and the Customize Chrome panel loses its
Google entry points.
